; claude: Scratch's language (Mitchel Resnick's Lifelong Kindergarten
; group, MIT Media Lab, 2007): the blocks as one table of specs, as
; Scratch 3's opcodes are (Scratch_blocks); their text, the
; scratchblocks notation of the Scratch forums and wiki, read and
; printed (Scratch_text); and a project run, sprites on a stage, each
; script a thread that yields at the end of every loop's turn
; (Scratch_run). Used by TinyScratch (apps/devtools/), whose editor is
; appkits/blocks. No Playground: the stage is numbers, the app draws
; it. A private library, installed as part of elm_playground: pure
; OCaml.
(library
 (name scratch)
 (package elm_playground)
 (wrapped false)
)
